---- what it raises, and what it is given
object KeyError: ('from __call__', (1,)) True 50 RecursionError: maximum recursion depth  [(1, 2, 3), "TypeError: <lambda>() missing 1 required positional argument: 'a'", "TypeError: <lambda>() missing 1 required keyword-only argument: 'c'", 'TypeError: <lambda>() takes from 2 to 3 positional arguments but 4 positional arguments (and 1 keyword-only argument) were given', "TypeError: <lambda>() got an unexpected keyword argument 'd'", "TypeError: <lambda>() got multiple values for argument 'a'"]
tuple KeyError: ('from __call__', (1,)) True 50 RecursionError: maximum recursion depth  [(1, 2, 3), "TypeError: <lambda>() missing 1 required positional argument: 'a'", "TypeError: <lambda>() missing 1 required keyword-only argument: 'c'", 'TypeError: <lambda>() takes from 2 to 3 positional arguments but 4 positional arguments (and 1 keyword-only argument) were given', "TypeError: <lambda>() got an unexpected keyword argument 'd'", "TypeError: <lambda>() got multiple values for argument 'a'"]
